======================================================================================================================
PART VI -- THE HOLES, with sizes.  Nothing here is written as an open question.
======================================================================================================================

    H-A  THE CLUSTER DEFICIT (the big one)
      The residual behaves like MASS in BOTH dynamics and lensing, so no lensing-sector repair can reach it.
      SIZE: required/delivered mass at each cluster's own R500 = 1.618 +/- 0.022 (canonical) / 1.493 +/- 0.020 (alt)
      against the hydrostatic mass, and 1.987 +/- 0.246 / 1.834 +/- 0.227 against weak lensing; the two agree
      (S_lens - S_dyn = +0.37 +/- 0.24, 1.55 sigma).  In raw Delta Sigma over 0.5-2 Mpc the framework is short
      by 2.5-2.7x and its log-slope is +0.53 +/- 0.06 SHALLOWER, a 9 sigma SHAPE error, because its phantom is a
      near-uniform sheet.  The acceleration excess at 40 kpc is 3.37 a0, 5.2x the kernel's own hard ceiling, which
      no interpolation function can absorb.  The required source is 6.8x the baryons with rho ~ r^-1.53.
      MECHANISMS CLOSED: interpolation kernel (A7, |z| = 13); fixed-strength finite-range force (A7, BBN 41x);
      screened force in Phi, rho or M (A7, 12.8 sigma overlap + cosmological ordering); hydrostatic bias (A18 -- the
      required b is NEGATIVE, -0.82, against a measured [0, +0.42]); the curl field (A25 -- real but exactly
      invisible to the radial average, closes 3.9% of the gap and runs the wrong way); a late-time roll (A16 --
      buys the cosmology but gives 0.97 of the required 2.2-5.1 contrast); light thermal relics (Tremaine-Gunn,
      m >= 4.67 eV, and the N_eff/RAR pincer at 27.6 vs 11 eV); wave dark matter (pincer with no interior, 1.4x);
      four condensate constructions; the environment switch.  AND the ratio is NOT MONOTONE in scale: binary
      galaxies need 30.9 +/- 1.6 within the pair separation against 5.73 +/- 0.68 at 0.80 R500, 5.7x and 16 sigma.
      WHAT IS LEFT: a cold, baryon-tracing component -- i.e. cold dark matter.  The theory does not contain one.

    H-B  NO DARK SECTOR AT ALL, hence no CMB and no structure
      Removing the condensate is what cures the clock tachyon (A13/L14), and it was the action's only dark component.
      SIZE: the condensate's dark fraction is capped at 2.6e-6 against Omega_d = 0.266, short by 1.0e5x.  With it
      gone the theory has baryons only; the CMB third peak, S_8 and the matter power spectrum are unaddressed.
      The linear MOND source that might have regenerated P(k) does not: at linear order the causal boost leaves
      sigma_8 <= 0.65 with a 20-2000x deficit at k = 0.5-1 h/Mpc, at any |K_2| (A/g04h).

    H-C  kappa = 1/2 IS FITTED
      a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) is dimensionally forced; kappa is not.  SIZE: A24/L32 T1 proves kappa is a ZERO
      MODE of any local action of this class -- F -> F + C is exactly degenerate with Lambda -- so no member of the
      class can derive it.  Deriving it reduces to fixing one number, beta/sqrt(Ztilde) = kappa/sqrt2 = 0.354.
      Twenty-seven simple numbers lie inside the measured 3 sigma band; landing there is not evidence.

    H-D  THE FOLIATION'S ONE ESCAPE IS UNDECIDED
      A26/L31 proves Lorentz invariance XOR two modes under a LOCALITY hypothesis, verified against a 17-theory table
      with no counterexample.  Hypothesis (iv), locality, is NOT proved: temporal nonlocality is a live escape
      (holding g_ext fixed, pushing the source 1000x drops every local invariant 1000x while |grad(box^-1 R)| is
      exactly constant).  A parallel lane is deciding it with a Hamiltonian mode count for retarded-nonlocal
      gravity.  IF that escape opens, the preferred foliation this theory is built on is a CHOICE, not a theorem.

    H-E  THE IC <-> ACTION MAPPING IS NOT PUBLISHED (challenge B2)
      c_14 has three inconsistent readings in the lead's files spanning 0.073-1.333, and c_2 vanishes at the witness
      where the mode was measured.  SIZE: the identification sigma = (2-c_14)c_2/[c_14(2+3c_2)] used above -- the
      one that tightens c_14 to 2.0e-6 -- is therefore STATED, not proved.  The region is non-empty with or
      without it (PART IV, T4), so nothing structural depends on it; the SHARPNESS of the c_14 bound does.

    H-F  c_2 SITS FIVE ORDERS BELOW THE CERTIFIED HEALTHY RANGE
      f34b certifies the scalar sector's linear health for c_2 in [0.01, 0.1].  The assembled point has c_2 = 1.7e-6.
      SIZE: 5 orders of magnitude of untested parameter.  Not a computed failure -- a gate nobody has run.

    H-G  TWO DOCUMENTATION CONFLICTS ARE STILL OPEN
      (i) the kernel: recipe ingredient I1 freezes mu = 1 - e^-y, THE_ACTION section 3 carries nu_RAR; they differ by
      up to 0.073 dex and the exponential ceiling is exceeded 5x more often on the bulgeless SPARC control.
      (ii) xi: THE_ACTION's section-2 table still quotes 0.03/0.05 pc, the UNSATURATED partner's floors, against
      section 5.13 and A33's 0.10/0.15 pc for the kernel a scalar can actually carry.  One document each must be
      amended; until then any cross-document comparison is ill-defined.

    H-H  STANDING LIABILITIES NOT REPAIRED BY THE ASSEMBLY
      Coma ultra-diffuse galaxies: amplitude +1.196 dex (factor 14) at 4.9 sigma against a 0.227 dex coherent systematic
      floor -- never quote the retracted 19.4 sigma.  The a0 ladder spans 0.78 dex across system classes.  Unequal-mass
      wide binaries: a resolution-independent common-mode force is an open numerical item.  Non-spherical accretion
      and the existence theory of the non-spherical fourth-order law are untouched.
  [FAIL] T8 the theory has no unaddressed hole larger than a factor of two   (it has: the cluster mass deficit is a factor 1.49-1.99 AND a 9 sigma shape error AND 5.2x the kernel's own ceiling at 40 kpc, and there is no dark component in the action at all (short by 1.0e5x))

======================================================================================================================
PART VII -- WHAT IS DISTINCTIVE, WITH NUMBERS, AND WHAT WOULD FALSIFY IT.
======================================================================================================================

    P1  THE BOUNDED BOOST -- a hard, parameter-free ceiling dark matter cannot impose
      g_obs - g_bar <= C a0 = 0.6476 a0 = 6.063e-11 / 7.304e-11 m/s^2, EVERYWHERE, in EVERY system,
      with no free parameter.  A halo's g_halo is set by M_200 and c, which span decades and are not tied to a0.
      FALSIFIED BY: one system, with a trustworthy baryon model, above the ceiling.  Currently 99.23% of 2352 SPARC
      points obey it; the 18 >3 sigma exceptions are in five named galaxies, 13 of them in NGC5985.

    P2  a0(z): the surviving distinctive prediction
      The deep-MOND baryonic-Tully-Fisher zero point is FLAT to <1% out to z = 5 on the derived law, against LambdaCDM's
      +0.33 dex by z = 2.5 and +0.576 dex at the same redshift for a rising-a0 reading.  DECISIVE MEASUREMENT:
      a deep-MOND lensed rotator at z ~ 2-2.5 measured to +/- 0.13 dex.  This, not kappa, is the discriminator.

    P3  GAIA DR4 WIDE BINARIES -- registered, and it is a NEWTON-LIKE answer
      gamma_v <= 1.0450 (canonical, xi = 0.10 pc) / 1.0300 (alt, xi = 0.15 pc), falling toward 1 as xi grows, against
      Arm A's registered band 1.16-1.23 and Newton's 1.000.  These are CEILINGS: DR4 can kill this arm from above,
      it cannot confirm it over Newton.  A measurement inside 1.16-1.23 falsifies the coherence-length structure.

    P4  THE CLUSTER PEAK RADIUS is mass-independent (conditional on a dust sector existing)
      If any component with the scalar's stiffness supplies part of the residual, its peak radius is set by
      H = 0.42 e c^2/(|K_2| a0) alone and is therefore the SAME PHYSICAL RADIUS in every cluster, where an NFW scale
      radius grows as M^(1/3).  NOTE: the assembled theory has no such component, so this is a prediction of the
      condensate branch that was REMOVED, and is listed to be honest about what removing it costs.

    P5  THE SADDLE NULL
      No Bekenstein-Magueijo anomaly at any Solar-System field null: the coherence operator erases it by 1e-29.  LISA
      Pathfinder-class saddle flybys would see nothing.  A detection falsifies the operator.

    P6  THE CARRIER/AQUAL FORK, newly priced here
      The two structures agree below s = 0.63 and diverge above it, reaching 0.073 dex.  At s = 3 the carrier
      predicts Delta = 0.648 and AQUAL 0.136, a 0.066 dex difference in g.  BIG-SPARC's transition
      bins decide which structure the data prefer -- and only the carrier arm needs the coherence length at all.

    P7  THE SATURATION EXPONENT is bounded above
      p <= 1.7538: the kernel's approach to its ceiling is a POWER LAW, never exponential.  Measuring the approach faster
      than Delta = C[1 - (s0/s)^1.754] falsifies the perturbative existence of the theory's own cubic action.

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
    The admissible region is NON-EMPTY.  An explicit point is exhibited above and passes eleven gates on
    both footings.  Every LOCAL test the programme owns -- Cassini, the Saturn phantom mass, the sunward
    anomaly, alpha_1, alpha_2, alpha_3, gamma, the tensor speed, the degree-of-freedom count and its health,
    Hadamard well-posedness, causality, black holes, galactic rotation curves and the lensing-dynamics slip --
    passes at that point, on both footings.  That is a real result and it is the first time the programme has
    had one simultaneously.

    Every test at a scale ABOVE a galaxy fails, and they all fail for ONE reason: removing the condensate --
    which is what cures the clock tachyon, the single gate in every minimal incompatible subset L14 found --
    leaves the action with no dark component at all.  The cluster deficit is a factor 1.49-1.99 in mass at
    R500 in both dynamics and lensing, with a 9 sigma shape error in Delta Sigma and an acceleration excess
    5.2x the kernel's own hard ceiling at 40 kpc; the CMB, S_8 and the matter power spectrum are unaddressed.

    So: this is a complete, internally consistent, Solar-System-safe, galaxy-correct relativistic theory of
    gravity with a preferred foliation and four healthy propagating modes -- and it is not a complete theory
    of the universe, because it needs a cold, baryon-tracing component that it does not contain and that
    every mechanism it does contain has been shown, one by one, unable to supply.
  [FAIL] V1 [THE VERDICT] this is a complete theory   (it is a complete theory of GRAVITY at Solar-System and galaxy scales with a non-empty parameter region, and an INCOMPLETE theory of the universe: it requires a cold dark component it does not contain.  What is missing is exactly that component, plus a derivation of kappa, plus the locality hypothesis of the foliation theorem.)
  [PASS] V2 the parameter space of the assembled theory is non-empty under the corrected constraints -- THE question this lane was opened to answer   (YES: grid 76,240 / 57,180 points, plus a derived explicit point admitted on both footings, with the clock tachyon gate satisfied IDENTICALLY because Q_0 = 0)

RESULT: 4 FAIL -> ['T5 no two settled results constrain the same parameter inconsistently', 'T7 the assembled theory passes every gate at scales ABOVE a galaxy', 'T8 the theory has no unaddressed hole larger than a factor of two', 'V1 [THE VERDICT] this is a complete theory']
  (FAILs T5, T7, T8, V1 and F-lines are RESULTS, not machine errors: they record the cluster deficit,
   the absent dark sector, the two documentation conflicts and the incompleteness.  Every CONTROL --
   K1-K9, N1-N7, T1, T2 -- must pass for the rest to mean anything.)
